phonetic_matching_system.output_format:
For each word pair comparison, provide a JSON response:

{
  "score": 0.90,
  "level": "perfect_match",
  "reasoning": {
    "prosodic": "Both paroxítonas ✓, same syllable count (3) ✓, stress position 2 ✓ → FULL PROSODIC MATCH",
    "tonic_core": "Tonic syllable 'ca' completely identical ✓✓✓ → PERFECT CORRESPONDENCE",
    "phonetic": "Vowel sequence e-a-o identical ✓✓, ending -ato/-ado very similar ✓ → STRONG",
    "morphological": "Shared prefix 're-' ✓, similar suffixes -ato/-ado ✓ → GOOD COHERENCE"
  },
  "score_breakdown": {
    "prosodic": 0.25,
    "tonic_core": 0.45,
    "phonetic": 0.15,
    "morphological": 0.05
  },
  "explanation": "Near-perfect match. The identical tonic syllable 'ca' creates a very strong rhyme. Full prosodic correspondence means they flow identically in verse. The shared prefix 're-' adds morphological coherence. Only difference is the final consonant (t vs d), which is minimal. This would be an excellent rhyme in any poetic context.",
  "poetic_quality": "Would create excellent rhyme in traditional poetry, MPB, or any verse form",
  "native_speaker_assessment": "Native PT-BR speakers would immediately recognize this as a strong rhyme"
}
